==Spanish==

===Letter===
{{infl|es|letter|lower case||upper case|CH|mixed case|Ch}}

# ''[[che]]'', the fourth letter of the Spanish alphabet, after {{term|c}} and before {{term|d}}

====Usage notes====
Since 1994, this letter has been treated as {{term|c}} followed by {{term|h}} for collation (sorting) purposes only.  Otherwise, it is still considered a distinct letter of the Spanish alphabet.

----

==Welsh==

===Letter===
{{infl|cy|letter|lower case||upper case|CH|mixed case|Ch}}

# ''[[èch]]'', the fourth letter of the Welsh alphabet, after {{term|c}} and before {{term|d}}

====Usage notes====
Lke the other Welsh digraphs, {{term|ch}} is considered a distinct letter of the Welsh alphabet for all purposes, including collation.  Thus, {{term|chwech}} is alphabetically sorted '''after''' {{term|cyllell}}.

